@label sct:113343008 "Body organ structure (body structure)"
@ann sct:113343008 skos:altLabel "Body organ"
@ann sct:113343008 skos:definition "An anatomical structure that consists of the maximal set of organ parts so connected to one another that together they constitute a self-contained unit of macroscopic anatomy, distinct both morphologically and functionally from other such units. Together with other organs, an organ constitutes an organ system or a body part. An organ is divisible into organ parts but not organs (examples: femur, biceps, liver, heart, aorta, sciatic nerve, ovary)."
@ann sct:113343008 skos:prefLabel "Body organ structure"
